Z||000003||Elvira||08-27-2001||09:04 PM||||We have that one on Chester's 86GT.  We pulled a 5'x8' trailer from NH to Bob Schlag's place in PA and back in one day (1020miles) with no problem at all.  It was empty there, but lots of parts in it on the trip back.  We are quite happy with it and it is almost invisible!  Hope this helps!!<P>------------------<BR>Elvira<BR>Blue 87GT<BR>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles||||reg||7
Z||000004||mrfiero||08-27-2001||11:56 PM||||I have logged over 20,000 miles towing cars with a Fiero using the Fiero Store hitch with no problems.<P>All of my trips were cross country odysseys that were over 2000 miles (one trip was 8000!).<P>It is true that the Fiero isn't the ideal tow vehicle, but it can handle it.  It sounds like your trips will be short, so that's even better.  ||||reg||1
